Dear Ruth,

Thank you for sending Coastline's data processing addendum. Comments below; the marked-up copy is attached (Coastline_Tessera_DPA_WSGR_comments_2026-03-08.docx).

1. Section 3 (sub-processors): Coastline's draft requires written consent for each new sub-processor. We have changed this to notice plus a 30-day objection right, which matches what Tessera has with Halberd and Northstar. Please confirm the current sub-processor list (Google Cloud, Sentry, and the email provider, I believe) so Annex 2 is accurate.
2. Section 6 (breach notification): 24 hours as drafted is shorter than Tessera can reliably commit to; we have proposed 72 hours from confirmation, consistent with your other agreements.
3. Section 9 (audit): limited to once per year on 30 days' notice, at Coastline's cost.
4. Everything else is acceptable as sent.

Apologies for the Sunday email; I wanted you to have this before your call with Coastline on Monday.

Kind regards,

